  "ai_overview": {
    "text_blocks": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Your roof likely needs replacement if it is over 20 years old, sags, or loses heavy granules into the gutters.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "over 20 years old, sags, or loses heavy granules into the gutters"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Age and Exterior Signs"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Old Age: Most asphalt shingle roofs last 20 to 25 years."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Curling Shingles: Edges turning upward mean the shingles suffer from heat or moisture damage."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Granule Loss: Finding lots of tiny colored sand grains in your gutters means the protective UV layer is gone."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Missing Shingles: High winds or old age can tear shingles off, leaving the wood deck open to rain and snow."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Watch this short video to see visual examples of the top warning signs that indicate your roof needs to be replaced:",
        "video": {
          "link": "https://www.youtube.com/shorts/RgeQGLvfGF0",
          "thumbnail": "https://serpapi.com/images/i/R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAP_______yH5BAEKAAEALAAAAAABAAEAAAICTAEAOw.gif"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Interior and Structural Signs"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Water Stains: Faint yellow or brown spots on your ceiling mean water is leaking through."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Daylight in the Attic: Seeing light peek through your roof boards means the wood is warped or broken."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Sagging Deck: A wavy or drooping roof line is a major structural warning."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Ice Dams: Utah winters cause ice dams that push water under shingles and into your home."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you want to move forward, tell me:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "How old is your current roof?"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Are you seeing leaks inside your home or just wear outside?"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "I can help you plan your next steps or find out what to look for next."
